"""heard-ui: a light overlay for heard. macOS, Windows, Linux (one Qt script).

A translucent, always-on-top bar that is excluded from screen sharing, with:
  - Start listening / Pause: capture happens only in between. Pause just pauses; the transcript stays on screen.
  - Stop recording: files the transcript shown in the library as a Markdown log, clears the view and pauses.
    Each log gets a title made from the transcript's own most prominent phrases (local keyword extraction;
    nothing is sent anywhere).
  - the transcript as it lands (the sentence in progress dimmed), search, Copy transcript (while a call is on screen)
  - Library: every logged call, with its text, Copy and Show in folder
  - a tray / menu bar icon that shows whether capture is on

Global hotkeys: ⌘⇧H show/hide, ⌘⇧L start/pause (Ctrl+Shift on Windows). None on Linux.
Everything reads ~/.local/share/heard (heard.db, live.json, paused, daemon.alive); nothing leaves the machine.
"""
